      "artist": "NateBergin",
      "credit": "Own work",
      "source": "1st Glorious Mystery Stained Glass Window (Resurrection) Cathedral of the Madeleine Salt Lake City",
      "description": "The east transept window at the Cathedral of the Madeline in Salt Lake City was installed in 1908 by F. X. Zettler of the House of Littler, Royal Bavarian Institute in Munich. It is the first in a set of five windows depicting the Glorious Mysteries of the Rosary along the east side of the Cathedral. The window also depicts various saints clockwise from the top: Saint Francis de Sales, Saint Agnes of Rome, Saint Stephen, Saint Ignatius of Loyola, Saint Francis of Assisi, Saint Bernard of Clairvaux, Saint Vincent de Paul, and Saint Monica.",
